          "subject": "Chemistry",
          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry",
          "topic": "Mole concept and amount of substance",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "A mole is an amount of substance containing Avogadro's number of specified entities, approximately 6.022 × 10^23. The entities may be atoms, molecules, ions, or other stated particles. The amount in moles is n = mass/molar mass; particle count is then n times Avogadro's constant.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-chemistry-11",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-chemistry-043",
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
