          "subject": "Chemistry",
          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry",
          "topic": "Mole concept and amount of substance",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "For 18 g of water, using molar mass 18 g/mol, n = 18/18 = 1 mol. This sample contains about 6.022 × 10^23 water molecules and twice as many hydrogen atoms.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-chemistry-11",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-chemistry-043",
