          "subject": "Chemistry",
          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Classification of Elements and Periodicity",
          "topic": "Atomic radius and ionization enthalpy trends",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "Compare Na and Cl in Period 3. Both have valence electrons in the third shell, but Cl has a greater nuclear charge with stronger effective attraction, so its atomic radius is generally smaller. Removing an electron from Cl also generally requires more energy than removing one from Na.",
