          "subject": "Chemistry",
          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Equilibrium",
          "topic": "Dynamic equilibrium and Le Chatelier's principle",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "For N2(g) + 3H2(g) ⇌ 2NH3(g), adding H2 at constant temperature makes the system shift toward NH3 as it responds to the disturbance. The value of Kc remains the same at that temperature, even though the equilibrium concentrations change.",
