          "topic": "Ionic and covalent bonding",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "In a simple Lewis picture of NaCl, sodium transfers one electron to chlorine, producing Na⁺ and Cl⁻. Their electrostatic attraction forms an ionic lattice; it is not a collection of isolated NaCl molecules in the solid.",
