          "topic": "VSEPR shapes and bond angles",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "VSEPR predicts approximate molecular shape by arranging electron domains around a central atom to reduce repulsion. Lone pairs generally repel more strongly than bonding pairs, so they can compress bond angles. Shape names describe atomic positions, not lone-pair positions.",
